    "updated_at": "2015-12-03T14:53:12Z",
    "body": "> Gecko's implementation appears to be a real File\n\nIt does?\n\n```\ndocument.createElement(\"canvas\").toBlob(function (arg) { alert(arg instanceof File); })\n```\n\nalerts false for me in Gecko.  And `FileCallback` in Gecko's IDL takes a `Blob` argument.\n\nIt's not clear to me what the intent here is; whether this started out as a `Blob` thing (hence the name) and then tried to get converted to a `File` or the other way around.  But I agree that the spec as it stands is underdefined; if it really means to produce `File` objects it needs to define the filename and whatnot.  But why should it produce `File` objects, exactly?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
